# Frontend (Vite) environment variables.
# Copy to .env or .env.production as needed. Vite only exposes vars prefixed
# with VITE_ to the client bundle.

# API base URL.
#
# - Empty (default): the bundle calls same-origin paths like '/api/v1/...'.
#   Vite dev proxy (vite.config.ts) routes /api → http://localhost:8000;
#   production web deployments use a reverse proxy / CDN rewrite to do the
#   same. This is the right setting for the normal web/PWA build.
#
# - Non-empty: the bundle calls '<base>/api/v1/...' absolute URLs. Required
#   for the Capacitor iOS/Android wrap because the WebView origin is
#   capacitor://localhost — same-origin paths can't reach the backend.
#   Example:
#     VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.lexy.example.com
#   The hosted backend must list the WebView origin(s) in its CORS_ORIGINS:
#     CORS_ORIGINS=https://app.example.com,capacitor://localhost,https://localhost
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
